### =============================================
### 1. Custom Domain Management
### =============================================

### 1.1 Register a new custom domain
# Replace "your-real-domain.com" with a real domain you control, or a dummy domain if you plan to manually update the DB.
# @name registerDomain
POST {{host}}/v1/api/cms/domains
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domainName": "your-real-domain.com"
}

###

@domainId = {{registerDomain.response.body.data.domainId}}

### 1.2 List your custom domains
GET {{host}}/v1/api/cms/domains
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.3 Verify Domain Ownership (TXT Record)
# Before running this, add the TXT record shown in the register response to your domain's DNS settings.
# If you are testing locally without a real domain, you can manually update the DB:
# UPDATE custom_domains SET verification_status = 'VERIFIED' WHERE domain_id = 'YOUR_DOMAIN_ID';
POST {{host}}/v1/api/cms/domains/{{domainId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.4 Check DNS Pointing (A/CNAME Record)
# Before running this, ensure your domain points to the server IP/CNAME.
# If testing locally, update the DB manually:
# UPDATE custom_domains SET dns_status = 'POINTED' WHERE domain_id = 'YOUR_DOMAIN_ID';
POST {{host}}/v1/api/cms/domains/{{domainId}}/dns-check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.5 Activate the Domain
# Requires the domain to be both VERIFIED and POINTED.
PATCH {{host}}/v1/api/cms/domains/{{domainId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### =============================================
### 2. CMS Content Publishing
### =============================================

### 2.1 First, create a CMS Content piece to publish
# @name createContent
POST {{host}}/v1/api/cms/contents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Summer Sale 2026 Announcement",
  "contentBody": "<h2>Huge Summer Sale!</h2><p>Get up to 50% off on all items. Don't miss out.</p>",
  "contentType": "Article",
  "platform": "Web",
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}

###

@contentId = {{createContent.response.body.data.contentId}}

### 2.2 Publish the Content to the Custom Domain
POST {{host}}/v1/api/cms/contents/{{contentId}}/publish-domain
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domainId": "{{domainId}}",
  "slug": "summer-sale-2026",
  "summary": "Our biggest summer sale of the year is here!",
  "coverImageUrl": "https://example.com/images/summer-sale.jpg"
}

### 2.3 Get the Public URL for the Content
GET {{host}}/v1/api/cms/contents/{{contentId}}/public-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### =============================================
### 3. Public Route (Simulating a Facebook Crawler or Browser)
### =============================================

### 3.1 Fetch the published page via the Public Route
# Note: You MUST pass the "Host" header matching your registered domain.
GET {{host}}/p/haha/aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
Host: my-fake-site.com
